Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nPatients with a histologically or cytologically proven diagnosis of NSCLC \nUnresectable (locally advanced) stage IIIa or IIIb disease \nInitial radiotherapy field of treatment to encompass greater than or equal to 30% of the esophagus \nLife expectancy greater than or equal to 6 months \nEstimated weight loss less than or equal to 10% in the 3 months before study randomization \nMeasurable disease \n18 years of age or older \nEastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) performance status of 0 - 2 \nHemoglobin (hgb) greater than or equal to 10 g/dL without transfusional support or growth factor use in the 4 weeks before study randomization \nAbsolute neutrophil count (ANC) greater than or equal to 1.5 x 10^9/L without growth factor use in the 2 weeks before study randomization \nPlatelet count greater than or equal to 100 x 10^9/L \nSerum bilirubin less than or equal to 1.5 x institutional upper limit of normal (ULN) \nSerum creatinine less than or equal to 2.0 mg/dL (Note: Patients with a serum creatinine greater than or equal to 1.4 and less than or equal to 2.0 mg/dL must demonstrate a 24-hour urinary creatinine clearance greater than or equal to 50 mL/min) \nFemales of childbearing potential: negative serum or urine pregnancy test \nPatient must give written informed consent before participating in any study-specific procedure, randomization, or receiving investigational product. \nPatients with reproductive capability must agree to practice adequate contraception methods. \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n- Patients with a histologically [OR] or cytologically proven diagnosis of NSCLC\nUnresectable (locally advanced) stage IIIa [OR] or IIIb disease\nInitial radiotherapy field [AND] of treatment to encompass greater than [OR] or equal to 30% of the esophagus\nLife expectancy greater than or equal to 6 months\nEstimated weight loss less than or equal to 10% in the 3 months before study randomization\nMeasurable disease\n18 years of age or older\nEastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) performance status of 0 - 2\nHemoglobin (hgb) greater than or equal to 10 g/dL [NOT] without transfusional support [OR] or growth factor use in the 4 weeks before study randomization\nAbsolute neutrophil count (ANC) greater than or equal to 1.5 x 10^9/L [NOT] without growth factor use in the 2 weeks before study randomization\nPlatelet count greater than or equal to 100 x 10^9/L\nSerum bilirubin less than or equal to 1.5 x institutional upper limit of normal (ULN)\nSerum creatinine less than or equal to 2.0 mg/dL (Note: Patients with a serum creatinine greater than or equal to 1.4 [AND] and less than or equal to 2.0 mg/dL must demonstrate a 24-hour urinary creatinine clearance greater than or equal to 50 mL/min)\nFemales [AND] of childbearing potential: negative serum [OR] or urine pregnancy test\nPatient must give written informed consent before participating in any study-specific procedure, randomization, [OR] or receiving investigational product.\nPatients with reproductive capability must agree to practice adequate contraception methods.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
- Patients with a histologically [OR] or cytologically proven diagnosis of NSCLC
Unresectable (locally advanced) stage IIIa [OR] or IIIb disease
Initial radiotherapy field [AND] of treatment to encompass greater than [OR] or equal to 30% of the esophagus
Life expectancy greater than or equal to 6 months
Estimated weight loss less than or equal to 10% in the 3 months before study randomization
Measurable disease
18 years of age or older
Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) performance status of 0 - 2
Hemoglobin (hgb) greater than or equal to 10 g/dL [NOT] without transfusional support [OR] or growth factor use in the 4 weeks before study randomization
Absolute neutrophil count (ANC) greater than or equal to 1.5 x 10^9/L [NOT] without growth factor use in the 2 weeks before study randomization
Platelet count greater than or equal to 100 x 10^9/L
Serum bilirubin less than or equal to 1.5 x institutional upper limit of normal (ULN)
Serum creatinine less than or equal to 2.0 mg/dL (Note: Patients with a serum creatinine greater than or equal to 1.4 [AND] and less than or equal to 2.0 mg/dL must demonstrate a 24-hour urinary creatinine clearance greater than or equal to 50 mL/min)
Females [AND] of childbearing potential: negative serum [OR] or urine pregnancy test
Patient must give written informed consent before participating in any study-specific procedure, randomization, [OR] or receiving investigational product.
Patients with reproductive capability must agree to practice adequate contraception methods.
