Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nThe treating physician has chosen Ventavis as a suitable long-term treatment for the patient \nPatient with primary pulmonary hypertension (i.e. Idiopathic Pulmonary Arterial Hypertension or Familial Pulmonary Arterial Hypertension) and classified as NYHA functional class III (NYHA = New York Heart Association) \nNo prior treatment with Ventavis or other active treatments for primary pulmonary hypertension within 6 weeks of date of study inclusion (unless otherwise advised by Bayer Schering Pharma) \n\n\n### Response:\nThe treating physician has chosen Ventavis as a suitable long-term treatment for the patient \nPatient with primary pulmonary hypertension (i.e. Idiopathic Pulmonary Arterial Hypertension [OR] or Familial Pulmonary Arterial Hypertension) and classified as NYHA functional class III (NYHA = New York Heart Association) \n[NOT] No prior treatment with Ventavis [OR] or other active treatments for primary pulmonary hypertension within 6 weeks of date of study inclusion (unless otherwise advised by Bayer Schering Pharma)<|eot_id|>']
Response: The treating physician has chosen Ventavis as a suitable long-term treatment for the patient 
Patient with primary pulmonary hypertension (i.e. Idiopathic Pulmonary Arterial Hypertension [OR] or Familial Pulmonary Arterial Hypertension) and classified as NYHA functional class III (NYHA = New York Heart Association) 
[NOT] No prior treatment with Ventavis [OR] or other active treatments for primary pulmonary hypertension within 6 weeks of date of study inclusion (unless otherwise advised by Bayer Schering Pharma)
