antihypertensives.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nExclusion Criteria:\nAny condition/illness that may affect the study outcomes [OR] or would make participation potentially harmful such as pregnancy [OR] or breastfeeding, [OR] diabetes mellitus, [OR] heart disease, [OR] stroke, [OR] hypertension, [OR] malabsorption syndromes, [OR] GERD, [OR] a history of ulcer, according to a detailed medical history.\nAbnormal hepatic function (liver function test > twice the normal range), abnormal renal function (creatinine > 1.1 mg/dl), fasting plasma glucose  in the diabetic range (>/= 126 mg/dl), [OR] or blood pressure > 140/90 mmHg. \nPresent alcoholism [OR] or drug abuse [OR] or use of medications that could interfere with the treatment including bronchodilators, [OR] quinolone antibiotics, [OR] monoamine oxidase inhibitors, [OR] anxiolytics, [OR] ranitidine, [OR] corticosteroids, [OR] growth hormone, [OR] antihypertensives.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Exclusion Criteria:
Any condition/illness that may affect the study outcomes [OR] or would make participation potentially harmful such as pregnancy [OR] or breastfeeding, [OR] diabetes mellitus, [OR] heart disease, [OR] stroke, [OR] hypertension, [OR] malabsorption syndromes, [OR] GERD, [OR] a history of ulcer, according to a detailed medical history.
Abnormal hepatic function (liver function test > twice the normal range), abnormal renal function (creatinine > 1.1 mg/dl), fasting plasma glucose  in the diabetic range (>/= 126 mg/dl), [OR] or blood pressure > 140/90 mmHg. 
Present alcoholism [OR] or drug abuse [OR] or use of medications that could interfere with the treatment including bronchodilators, [OR] quinolone antibiotics, [OR] monoamine oxidase inhibitors, [OR] anxiolytics, [OR] ranitidine, [OR] corticosteroids, [OR] growth hormone, [OR] antihypertensives.
