File: NCT00312429_inc 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_half/NCT00312429_inc.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nDiagnosis reviewed at transplant center and confirmed to fit the criterion for high risk blood disease or cancer, as defined for the study \nEstimated life expectancy of at least 6 weeks following study entry \nCancer and Leukemia Group B (CALGB) performance status less than or equal to 2 \nWhite blood cell count, platelet, hematocrit, tuberculosis, aspartate aminotransferase (AST), alanine aminotransferase (ALT), alkaline phosphatase, creatinine, and HIV test results reviewed by transplant center \nMultiple gated acquisition (MUGA), echocardiogram, cardiac MRI, and/or pulmonary function tests (PFT) performed and reviewed by transplant center (for individuals with an ejection fraction and diffusing capacity [DLCO] of 40-50%, the appropriate cardiology or pulmonary consultations should be considered if the individual has severe heart or lung disease at the initiation of therapy) \nSufficient number of umbilical cord blood units available for transplantation \nIf female, willing to use contraception throughout the study \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n- Diagnosis reviewed at transplant center and confirmed to fit the criterion for high risk blood disease [OR] or cancer, as defined for the study \n- Estimated life expectancy of at least 6 weeks following study entry \n- Cancer and Leukemia Group B (CALGB) performance status less than or equal to 2 \n- White blood cell count, [OR] platelet, [OR] hematocrit, [OR] tuberculosis, [OR] aspartate aminotransferase (AST), alanine aminotransferase (ALT), alkaline phosphatase, [OR] creatinine, [OR] and HIV test results reviewed by transplant center \n- Multiple gated acquisition (MUGA), echocardiogram, [OR] cardiac MRI, [OR] and/or pulmonary function tests (PFT) performed and reviewed by transplant center (for individuals with an ejection fraction [OR] and diffusing capacity [DLCO] of 40-50%, the appropriate cardiology [OR] or pulmonary consultations should be considered if the individual has severe heart [OR] or lung disease at the initiation of therapy) \n- Sufficient number of umbilical cord blood units available for transplantation \n- If female, willing to use contraception throughout the study<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
- Diagnosis reviewed at transplant center and confirmed to fit the criterion for high risk blood disease [OR] or cancer, as defined for the study 
- Estimated life expectancy of at least 6 weeks following study entry 
- Cancer and Leukemia Group B (CALGB) performance status less than or equal to 2 
- White blood cell count, [OR] platelet, [OR] hematocrit, [OR] tuberculosis, [OR] aspartate aminotransferase (AST), alanine aminotransferase (ALT), alkaline phosphatase, [OR] creatinine, [OR] and HIV test results reviewed by transplant center 
- Multiple gated acquisition (MUGA), echocardiogram, [OR] cardiac MRI, [OR] and/or pulmonary function tests (PFT) performed and reviewed by transplant center (for individuals with an ejection fraction [OR] and diffusing capacity [DLCO] of 40-50%, the appropriate cardiology [OR] or pulmonary consultations should be considered if the individual has severe heart [OR] or lung disease at the initiation of therapy) 
- Sufficient number of umbilical cord blood units available for transplantation 
- If female, willing to use contraception throughout the study
