History of diseases with influence on bone metabolism such as Paget's disease [OR] and primary hyperparathyroidism 
Severe physical [OR] or psychological concomitant diseases that might impair compliance with the provisions of the study protocol or that might impair the assessment of drug [OR] or patient safety, e.g. clinically significant ascites, [OR] cardiac failure, [OR] NYHA III or IV, clinically relevant pathologic findings in ECG 
Known hypersensitivity to zoledronic acid [OR] or other bisphosphonates 
Use of other investigational drugs 30 days prior to the date of randomization 
Known history [OR] or present abuse of alcohol [OR] or drugs 
Subjects who, in the opinion of the investigator, are unlikely to cooperate fully during the study 
Current active dental problems including infection of the teeth [OR] or jawbone (maxilla [OR] or mandibular); dental [OR] or fixture trauma, [OR] or a current [OR] or prior diagnosis of osteonecrosis of the jaw (ONJ), of exposed bone in the mouth, [OR] or of slow healing after dental procedures. 
Recent (within 6 weeks) [OR] or planned dental [OR] or jaw surgery (e.g. extraction, [OR] implants) 
Other protocol defined inclusion/exclusion criteria may apply.
