Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nSubjects not able to give informed consent \nLeft Bundle Branch Block \nThrombolytic therapy within 24 hours before randomization \nOral anticoagulation with International Normalized Ratio (INR) > 2 \nKnown platelets < 100.000/µl or known hemorrhagic diathesis \nStroke or Transient Ischemic Attack (TIA) within the past 6 months or any permanent residual neurological defect \nEvidence of an active gastrointestinal or urogenital bleeding \nMajor surgery within 6 weeks \nHistory of allergic reaction to abciximab or eptifibatide or any component used in the study (including contrast media) \nKnown severe renal (creatinine clearance <30ml/min) or hepatic insufficiency as well as Alanine transaminase (ALT)/aspartate transaminase (AST) elevations = 3xUpper limit normal (ULN); isolated AST-elevation is not considered an exclusion criteria from study participation \nSevere concomitant disease with life expectation < 1 year \nSubject has participated in any study using an investigational drug or device within 30 days or within 5 half-lives of the investigational drug (whichever is longer) of entry into this study. \nSubjects who will be inaccessible due to geographic or social factors during treatment or follow-up \nIn France, a subject is neither affiliated with nor a beneficiary of a social security category.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nExclusion Criteria:\nSubjects not able to give informed consent \nLeft Bundle Branch Block \nThrombolytic therapy within 24 hours before randomization \nOral anticoagulation [AND] with International Normalized Ratio (INR) > 2 \nKnown platelets < 100.000/µl [OR] or known hemorrhagic diathesis \nStroke [OR] or Transient Ischemic Attack (TIA) within the past 6 months [OR] or any permanent residual neurological defect \nEvidence of an active gastrointestinal [OR] or urogenital bleeding \nMajor surgery within 6 weeks \nHistory of allergic reaction to abciximab [OR] or eptifibatide [OR] or any component used in the study (including contrast media) \nKnown severe renal (creatinine clearance <30ml/min) [OR] or hepatic insufficiency [AND] as well as Alanine transaminase (ALT) [OR] /aspartate transaminase (AST) elevations = 3xUpper limit normal (ULN); isolated AST-elevation is not considered an exclusion criteria from study participation \nSevere concomitant disease [AND] with life expectation < 1 year \nSubject has participated in any study using an investigational drug [OR] or device within 30 days [OR] or within 5 half-lives of the investigational drug (whichever is longer) of entry into this study. \nSubjects who will be inaccessible due to geographic [OR] or social factors during treatment [OR] or follow-up \nIn France, a subject is neither affiliated with nor a beneficiary of a social security category.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Exclusion Criteria:
Subjects not able to give informed consent 
Left Bundle Branch Block 
Thrombolytic therapy within 24 hours before randomization 
Oral anticoagulation [AND] with International Normalized Ratio (INR) > 2 
Known platelets < 100.000/µl [OR] or known hemorrhagic diathesis 
Stroke [OR] or Transient Ischemic Attack (TIA) within the past 6 months [OR] or any permanent residual neurological defect 
Evidence of an active gastrointestinal [OR] or urogenital bleeding 
Major surgery within 6 weeks 
History of allergic reaction to abciximab [OR] or eptifibatide [OR] or any component used in the study (including contrast media) 
Known severe renal (creatinine clearance <30ml/min) [OR] or hepatic insufficiency [AND] as well as Alanine transaminase (ALT) [OR] /aspartate transaminase (AST) elevations = 3xUpper limit normal (ULN); isolated AST-elevation is not considered an exclusion criteria from study participation 
Severe concomitant disease [AND] with life expectation < 1 year 
Subject has participated in any study using an investigational drug [OR] or device within 30 days [OR] or within 5 half-lives of the investigational drug (whichever is longer) of entry into this study. 
Subjects who will be inaccessible due to geographic [OR] or social factors during treatment [OR] or follow-up 
In France, a subject is neither affiliated with nor a beneficiary of a social security category.
