File: NCT00426751_inc 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_half/NCT00426751_inc.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nWomen must be postmenopausal (i.e.12 months without menstrual period), or surgically sterile, i.e. women of child bearing potential are not allowed to be included into the study. In cases of doubt a pregnancy test should be performed. (NB -post menopausal women currently receiving hormone replacement are permissible) \nAcute myocardial infarction < 12 h defined as: \n1. Angina or equivalent symptoms > 20 min and \n2. ST elevation in 2 contiguous ECG leads (= 2 mm precordial lead, = 1 mm limb lead). This ECG recording serves as baseline ECG, i.e. ECG I. \nPlanned primary percutaneous coronary intervention \nThe subject has given written informed, dated consent to participate in the study \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nWomen must be postmenopausal ([OR] i.e.12 months [NOT] without menstrual period), [OR] or surgically sterile, [AND] i.e. women [AND] of child bearing potential are [NOT] not allowed to be included into the study. In cases of doubt a pregnancy test should be performed. (NB -post menopausal women currently receiving hormone replacement are permissible) \nAcute myocardial infarction < 12 h defined as: \n1. Angina [OR] or equivalent symptoms > 20 min [AND] and \n2. ST elevation in 2 contiguous ECG leads (= 2 mm precordial lead, = 1 mm limb lead). This ECG recording serves as baseline ECG, i.e. ECG I. \nPlanned primary percutaneous coronary intervention \nThe subject has given written informed, dated consent to participate in the study<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Women must be postmenopausal ([OR] i.e.12 months [NOT] without menstrual period), [OR] or surgically sterile, [AND] i.e. women [AND] of child bearing potential are [NOT] not allowed to be included into the study. In cases of doubt a pregnancy test should be performed. (NB -post menopausal women currently receiving hormone replacement are permissible) 
Acute myocardial infarction < 12 h defined as: 
1. Angina [OR] or equivalent symptoms > 20 min [AND] and 
2. ST elevation in 2 contiguous ECG leads (= 2 mm precordial lead, = 1 mm limb lead). This ECG recording serves as baseline ECG, i.e. ECG I. 
Planned primary percutaneous coronary intervention 
The subject has given written informed, dated consent to participate in the study
