struction:\nCreate an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before words like or, and/or, and / or in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like with, who, in addition, plus, and, but, that, despite, having.\n- Always write a [NOT] before no, not, none, don\'t, free, prevent, Inability, lack, impossible, off, without, unable, naive, excluded, absence\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\n  -  Patients with treatment-resistant schizophrenia\nExclusion Criteria:\n  -  Patients who have cominication with other psychiatric disease\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n - Patients with treatment-resistant schizophrenia\nExclusion Criteria:\n - Patients who have cominication with other psychiatric disease<|eot_id|>']
