Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_half/NCT00527826_exc.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nKnown other respiratory disorders or signs for other respiratory disorders (e.g. asthma, lung cancer, sarcoidosis, tuberculosis, lung fibrosis, cystic fibrosis, bronchoectasis). \nKnown history of significant inflammatory disease, other than COPD (e.g. rheumatoid arthritis and systemic lupus erythematosus). \nKnown to be severely alpha-1-antitrypsin deficient (PI SZ or ZZ) \nHaving undergone lung surgery (e.g. lung resection including lung volume reduction surgery, lung transplant) or subjects scheduled for surgery. \nConcurrent medication from Visit 1 and for the duration of the study with any of the prohibited medications: monoamine oxidase inhibitors and tricyclic antidepressants, and ritonavir (a highly potent cytochrome P450 3A4 inhibitor). \nSubjects receiving chronic or prophylactic antibiotic therapy. \nSerious, uncontrolled disease (including serious psychological disorders) likely to interfere with the study or impact on subject safety. \nHave, in the opinion of the investigator, evidence of alcohol, drug or solvent abuse. \nHistory of depression. \nHistory or presence of clinically significant drug sensitivity or clinically significant allergic reaction to corticosteroids or salmeterol. \nModerate or severe COPD exacerbation (requiring corticosteroids or increased dosage of corticosteroids and/or antibiotics or hospitalization) within the 4 weeks prior to Visit 1 \nLower respiratory tract infection within the 4 weeks prior to Visit 1. \nPregnant or lactating female and female of childbearing potential. \nSubject is a participating investigator, sub-investigator, study coordinator, or other employee of a participating investigator, or is an immediate family member of the before mentioned. Subject is an employee of GlaxoSmithKline (GSK). \nSubject participated in an investigational drug study within 30 days prior to Visit 1       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n  -  Subjects must have a diagnosis of COPD based on symptoms and spirometry\nExclusion Criteria:\n- Known other respiratory disorders [OR] or signs for other respiratory disorders (e.g. asthma, [OR] lung cancer, [OR] sarcoidosis, [OR] tuberculosis, [OR] lung fibrosis, [OR] cystic fibrosis, [OR] bronchoectasis). \nKnown history of significant inflammatory disease, other than COPD (e.g. rheumatoid arthritis [OR] and systemic lupus erythematosus). \nKnown to be severely alpha-1-antitrypsin deficient (PI SZ [OR] or ZZ) \nHaving undergone lung surgery (e.g. lung resection including lung volume reduction surgery, [OR] lung transplant) [OR] or subjects scheduled for surgery. \nConcurrent medication from Visit 1 and for the duration of the study with any of the prohibited medications: monoamine oxidase inhibitors [OR] and tricyclic antidepressants, [OR] and ritonavir (a highly potent cytochrome P450 3A4 inhibitor). \nSubjects receiving chronic [OR] or prophylactic antibiotic therapy. \nSerious, uncontrolled disease (including serious psychological disorders) likely to interfere with the study [OR] or impact on subject safety. \nHave, in the opinion of the investigator, evidence of alcohol, [OR] drug [OR] or solvent abuse. \nHistory of depression. \nHistory [OR] or presence of clinically significant drug sensitivity [OR] or clinically significant allergic reaction to corticosteroids [OR] or salmeterol. \nModerate [OR] or severe COPD exacerbation (requiring corticosteroids [OR] or increased dosage of corticosteroids [OR] and/or antibiotics [OR] or hospitalization) within the 4 weeks prior to Visit 1 \nLower respiratory tract infection within the 4 weeks prior to Visit 1. \nPregnant [OR] or lactating female [OR] and female of childbearing potential. \nSubject is a participating investigator, sub-investigator, study coordinator, or other employee of a participating investigator, or is an immediate family member of the before mentioned. Subject is an employee of GlaxoSmithKline (GSK). \nSubject participated in an investigational drug study within 30 days prior to Visit 1<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
  -  Subjects must have a diagnosis of COPD based on symptoms and spirometry
Exclusion Criteria:
- Known other respiratory disorders [OR] or signs for other respiratory disorders (e.g. asthma, [OR] lung cancer, [OR] sarcoidosis, [OR] tuberculosis, [OR] lung fibrosis, [OR] cystic fibrosis, [OR] bronchoectasis). 
Known history of significant inflammatory disease, other than COPD (e.g. rheumatoid arthritis [OR] and systemic lupus erythematosus). 
Known to be severely alpha-1-antitrypsin deficient (PI SZ [OR] or ZZ) 
Having undergone lung surgery (e.g. lung resection including lung volume reduction surgery, [OR] lung transplant) [OR] or subjects scheduled for surgery. 
Concurrent medication from Visit 1 and for the duration of the study with any of the prohibited medications: monoamine oxidase inhibitors [OR] and tricyclic antidepressants, [OR] and ritonavir (a highly potent cytochrome P450 3A4 inhibitor). 
Subjects receiving chronic [OR] or prophylactic antibiotic therapy. 
Serious, uncontrolled disease (including serious psychological disorders) likely to interfere with the study [OR] or impact on subject safety. 
Have, in the opinion of the investigator, evidence of alcohol, [OR] drug [OR] or solvent abuse. 
History of depression. 
History [OR] or presence of clinically significant drug sensitivity [OR] or clinically significant allergic reaction to corticosteroids [OR] or salmeterol. 
Moderate [OR] or severe COPD exacerbation (requiring corticosteroids [OR] or increased dosage of corticosteroids [OR] and/or antibiotics [OR] or hospitalization) within the 4 weeks prior to Visit 1 
Lower respiratory tract infection within the 4 weeks prior to Visit 1. 
Pregnant [OR] or lactating female [OR] and female of childbearing potential. 
Subject is a participating investigator, sub-investigator, study coordinator, or other employee of a participating investigator, or is an immediate family member of the before mentioned. Subject is an employee of GlaxoSmithKline (GSK). 
Subject participated in an investigational drug study within 30 days prior to Visit 1
