Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\n1. Have dementia or delirium (as determined by the palliative care specialist) at study entry. \n2. Are pregnant \n3. Have been taking corticosteroids for longer than 48 hours. \n4. Have pulmonary edema, ascites or pitting edema on clinical examination. \n5. Are unable to walk. \n6. Have a history of serious adverse gastrointestinal events (i.e., bleeding or perforation),history of a coagulopathy or current anti-coagulant use. \n7. Have an ALT/AST>3x upper limit of normal. \n8. Patients on methotrexate. \n9. Patients taking melatonin receptor agonists (such as Rozerem® [ramelteon]).       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n  -  Have dementia [OR] or delirium (as determined by the palliative care specialist) at study entry. \nExclusion Criteria:\n 1. Are pregnant \n 2. Have been taking corticosteroids for longer than 48 hours. \n 3. Have pulmonary edema, [OR] ascites [OR] or pitting edema on clinical examination. \n 4. Are [NOT] unable to walk. \n 5. Have a history of serious adverse gastrointestinal events (i.e., bleeding [OR] or perforation),history of a coagulopathy [OR] or current anti-coagulant use. \n 6. Have an ALT/ [OR] AST>3x upper limit of normal. \n 7. Patients on methotrexate. \n 8. Patients taking melatonin receptor agonists (such as Rozerem® [ramelteon]).<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
  -  Have dementia [OR] or delirium (as determined by the palliative care specialist) at study entry. 
Exclusion Criteria:
 1. Are pregnant 
 2. Have been taking corticosteroids for longer than 48 hours. 
 3. Have pulmonary edema, [OR] ascites [OR] or pitting edema on clinical examination. 
 4. Are [NOT] unable to walk. 
 5. Have a history of serious adverse gastrointestinal events (i.e., bleeding [OR] or perforation),history of a coagulopathy [OR] or current anti-coagulant use. 
 6. Have an ALT/ [OR] AST>3x upper limit of normal. 
 7. Patients on methotrexate. 
 8. Patients taking melatonin receptor agonists (such as Rozerem® [ramelteon]).
