Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nAge less than 18 \nClinical or laboratory evidence of systemic infection \nCurrent pregnancy as assessed by preoperative urine HCG test \nSerious, uncontrolled, non-malignant illness \nMalignant illness requiring systemic chemotherapy in the last 6 months \nDocumented allergy to oxycodone, morphine sulfate or acetaminophen \nContraindication to peripheral nerve blockade or general anesthesia including: \n1. patient refusal \n2. active infection at site of planned block \n3. documented allergy to any local or general anesthetic medications \n4. significant coagulopathy( prothrombin time >15 seconds, INR>1.5 \n5. pre-existing neuropathy and medical conditions or deformities which would compromise block or anesthetic safety \nPlanned pleurodesis \nCurrent use of high dose inhaled or systemic steroids \nCurrent use of Amiodarone (Cordarone) \nMorbid obesity (BMI=40kg/m2) \nPatients with clinically significant mental health issues such as psychosis requiring treatment with antipsychotic medications. \nPatients unable to consent \nPatients with active infections requiring antibiotics within one month of registration \nParticipation in other clinical trials that may interfere with this study       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n  -  Currently enrolled within the "Peds ACL" study at MSCHON (will utilize the same inclusion and exclusion criteria as "Peds ACL" study)\nExclusion Criteria:\nAge less than 18 \nClinical [OR] or laboratory evidence of systemic infection \nCurrent pregnancy as assessed by preoperative urine HCG test \nSerious, uncontrolled, [NOT] non-malignant illness \nMalignant illness requiring systemic chemotherapy in the last 6 months \nDocumented allergy to oxycodone, [OR] morphine sulfate [OR] or acetaminophen \nContraindication to peripheral nerve blockade [OR] or general anesthesia including: \n1. patient refusal \n2. active infection at site of planned block \n3. documented allergy to any local [OR] or general anesthetic medications \n4. significant coagulopathy( prothrombin time >15 seconds, [OR] INR>1.5 \n5. pre-existing neuropathy [OR] and medical conditions [OR] or deformities which would compromise block [OR] or anesthetic safety \nPlanned pleurodesis \nCurrent use of high dose inhaled [OR] or systemic steroids \nCurrent use of Amiodarone (Cordarone) \nMorbid obesity (BMI=40kg/m2) \nPatients with clinically significant mental health issues such as psychosis requiring treatment with antipsychotic medications. \nPatients unable to consent \nPatients with active infections requiring antibiotics within one month of registration \nParticipation in other clinical trials that may interfere with this study<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
  -  Currently enrolled within the "Peds ACL" study at MSCHON (will utilize the same inclusion and exclusion criteria as "Peds ACL" study)
Exclusion Criteria:
Age less than 18 
Clinical [OR] or laboratory evidence of systemic infection 
Current pregnancy as assessed by preoperative urine HCG test 
Serious, uncontrolled, [NOT] non-malignant illness 
Malignant illness requiring systemic chemotherapy in the last 6 months 
Documented allergy to oxycodone, [OR] morphine sulfate [OR] or acetaminophen 
Contraindication to peripheral nerve blockade [OR] or general anesthesia including: 
1. patient refusal 
2. active infection at site of planned block 
3. documented allergy to any local [OR] or general anesthetic medications 
4. significant coagulopathy( prothrombin time >15 seconds, [OR] INR>1.5 
5. pre-existing neuropathy [OR] and medical conditions [OR] or deformities which would compromise block [OR] or anesthetic safety 
Planned pleurodesis 
Current use of high dose inhaled [OR] or systemic steroids 
Current use of Amiodarone (Cordarone) 
Morbid obesity (BMI=40kg/m2) 
Patients with clinically significant mental health issues such as psychosis requiring treatment with antipsychotic medications. 
Patients unable to consent 
Patients with active infections requiring antibiotics within one month of registration 
Participation in other clinical trials that may interfere with this study
