ondoms for the duration of the study. \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n- Histologically [OR] or cytologically confirmed adenocarcinoma of the breast [AND] with locally advanced [OR] or metastatic disease, [AND] and a candidate for chemotherapy.\n - HER2-positive.\n - [NOT] No prior chemotherapy for their metastatic breast cancer (MBC).\n - Measurable disease.\n - Age ≥ 18 years.\n - For women [AND] of childbearing potential [OR] and men [AND] with partners of childbearing potential, agreement to use a highly effective, [NOT] non-hormonal form of contraception [OR] or 2 effective forms of [NOT] non-hormonal contraception by the patient and/or partner. Contraception use must continue for the duration of study treatment [AND] and for at least 6 months after the last dose of study treatment. Male patients whose partners are pregnant should use condoms for the duration of the study.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
- Histologically [OR] or cytologically confirmed adenocarcinoma of the breast [AND] with locally advanced [OR] or metastatic disease, [AND] and a candidate for chemotherapy.
 - HER2-positive.
 - [NOT] No prior chemotherapy for their metastatic breast cancer (MBC).
 - Measurable disease.
 - Age ≥ 18 years.
 - For women [AND] of childbearing potential [OR] and men [AND] with partners of childbearing potential, agreement to use a highly effective, [NOT] non-hormonal form of contraception [OR] or 2 effective forms of [NOT] non-hormonal contraception by the patient and/or partner. Contraception use must continue for the duration of study treatment [AND] and for at least 6 months after the last dose of study treatment. Male patients whose partners are pregnant should use condoms for the duration of the study.
